 2. 🛰️ Voyager&#x27;s new record 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Rendering: NASA/JPL-Caltech At exactly 5:16:07 ET tomorrow morning, NASA's Voyager 1 spacecraft will become the first human-made object to reach one light-day from Earth, Alex Fitzpatrick writes. 

 At that distance — about 16 billion miles — it takes a full day for light (and thus radio transmissions and operator commands) to travel between Voyager and Earth. 🚀 Launched in 1977, humanity's most distant probe is still transmitting valuable data as it cruises along in interstellar space at nearly 38,000 mph.

 That's thanks to NASA's Voyager team, which keeps finding novel ways to keep the spacecraft operational. Go deeper . 

 
 
